# First deployment

Clone the repository and enter its root:

    git clone git@github.com:pbizopoulos/canonicalization ~/github.com/pbizopoulos/canonicalization/
    cd ~/github.com/pbizopoulos/canonicalization/

In the Hetzner project, upload the developer SSH public key under the name
`default`, then create an API token. Supply the token directly to OpenTofu:

    export TF_VAR_hcloud_token='<token>'
    nix run .#deploy_host_template

The package stores OpenTofu data and state under
`packages/deploy_host_template/tmp/`. The deployed server address is written to
`packages/deploy_host_template/prm/ipv4_address`. The default NixOS
configuration is `default`; all variables in `main.tf` remain overrideable with
the usual `TF_VAR_<name>` environment variables.

The selected Hetzner server type must satisfy the NixOS configuration's disk
and memory requirements. To delete the server, first disable deletion and
rebuild protection, then destroy it with OpenTofu or remove it through the
Hetzner console.
